      "taskId": "T3",
      "name": "form-fill",
      "description": "Navigate to https://www.selenium.dev/selenium/web/web-form.html, fill the text/password/textarea fields, pick a dropdown option, submit.",
      "charlotte": {
        "sequence": [
          "charlotte_navigate({ url })",
          "charlotte_observe({ detail: \"summary\" }) — discover all form field element_ids in one call.",
          "charlotte_type × 3 — text input, password, textarea.",
          "charlotte_select({ element_id, value: \"Two\" }) — native <select> dropdown; Charlotte exposes it as type=\"select\" with an options[] array, and charlotte_select works on it directly (verified empirically).",
          "charlotte_click(submit button \"Submit\") — NOT charlotte_submit: this form (like httpbin's) has no accessible name (no aria-label/title), so Chromium's accessibility tree never exposes it with role=\"form\", and Charlotte only recognizes forms via that AX role. No form_id is available for this page either — see the finding in tasks.md. The submit button is clicked directly instead."
        ],
